            <div class="col-lg-7 col-md-9">
                <div class="post-content">
                    <blockquote>We listened, read and watched how these majestic creatures conquered the sea. But what if we could experience sharks directly to prove the stories we’ve heard about so far?</blockquote>
                    <p><span class="firstcharacter">M</span>ost of us were raised with fascinating stories about sharks.They play a very important role in marine areas, sitting at the top of the food chain, and maintaining the delicate balance of marine life. We listened, read and watched how these majestic creatures conquered the sea. But what if we could experience sharks directly to prove the stories we’ve heard about so far? The first question coming to our mind most of the time would be regarding safety. Is it safe to dive around sharks? Sharks feed on fish, often attacking in schools. Attacks on humans occur when sharks are hungry, harassed, or, in some cases, defending their territory. It is known that many interactions with humans appear more likely to be due to mistaken identity. This is why it’s important for us to know the shark's routine.</p>
                    <p>Dawn and dusk are prime hunting time for many types of sharks. There is likely to be more shark activity on a dive, but, on the other hand it will be more risky for divers as they search for prey at those times of the day.</p>
                    <p>Sharks are naturally curious, not the horrible monsters portrayed in television and the movies. They might come to you when you are diving and then leave. Remember, they are natural predators and scavengers, not monsters of the deep. So what should we do when we encounter sharks? Swimming towards sharks will be one of the suggestions. Sharks know that prey does not swim toward it. The prey swim away quickly as they see sharks, if we do the opposite, sharks will turn away. </p>
                    <p>Humans are fairly large in the water and two together forms an even larger presence. This is why diving with instructors will make you feel more relaxed and comfortable around sharks. Moreover, instructors will help you when you’re nervous or in awe seeing this mesmerizing creature. </p>
                    <p>Respect them and they will respect us. Maintain distance with sharks and keep safe while diving. That is the mindset we need to follow when diving around these. Afterall, they are amazing creatures for you adventure seekers. Diving with sharks will be one of your bucket list that you shouldn’t miss! </p>
